    "release_url_pattern": "https://www.federalreserve.gov/releases/h8/YYYYMMDD/",
    "read_on": "2026-10-14"
  },
  "method": [
    "The 13 releases are the ones the due diligence (docs/research/h8-groups-due-diligence.md, section 3) found restating an earlier week of large and small domestic total assets by at least $50bn each, in opposite directions. Each release's archived page and the page of the release before it were fetched on 2026-10-14 and parsed with `repo_liquidity.h8.parse_group_lines`. `restated_weeks` lists the weeks of the four-week window whose large and small totals both moved by at least $50bn between the two pages.",
    "`release_sha256` is the digest of the page the tracked extract was cut from (releases record). `fetched_sha256` is the digest of the bytes fetched on 2026-10-14 for this record: the two differ for every page, because a saved page's digest identifies the fetch and not the release (issue #40). The group lines parsed from the fetched page equal the first-print values in the extract for every one of the 13 releases.",
    "`break_week` is the week first printed in that release: the first week of the first-print series on the new basis (the week before it was first printed in the release before, on the old one). The restated weeks show that the new basis reaches back at least to the first of them; no note dates it.",
    "A cause is `cited` only where a note of the H.8 'Notes on Data' page or a note on the archived release page states it, quoted verbatim with its as-of date. No move is labelled from memory. The archived release pages carry one general footnote on the large and small groups being adjusted for 'mergers and panel shifts between these two bank groups' and name no event; it is not a cause of any move."
  ],
